chapter.v:
	from Sihor, 

	 which is east of Egypt, as far as the border of Ekron northward (which is counted as Canaanite); the five lords of the Philistines—the Gazites, the Ashdodites, the Ashkelonites, the Gittites, and the Ekronites; also the Avites;
 [Josh. 18:13; 1 Kin. 9:17; 2 Chr. 8:5 d Josh. 21:21; 1 Kin. 9:15; 1 Chr.]

	from the 

	 south, all the land of the Canaanites, and Mearah that belongs to the Sidonians as far as Aphek, to the border of the Amorites;
 [Josh. 17:14]

	the land 

	 of the Gebalites, and all Lebanon, toward the sunrise, from Baal Gad below Mount Hermon as far as the entrance to Hamath;
 [Josh. 18:13 h 2 Chr. 8:5] [Judg. 1:29; 1 Chr. 7:28,]

	from Aroer 

	 which is on the bank of the River Arnon, and the town that is in the midst of the ravine, and all the plain of Medeba as far as Dibon;
 [Josh. 17:9]
